.Dd May 27, 2026
.Dt PROBS 7
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm probs
.Nd a small Codeforces workbench
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a directory convention and a set of short commands for solving
Codeforces problems in C++.
It is intentionally plain.
A solution is a file, a test is a pair of files, and a build product is
kept out of the way.
.Pp
Problem names have the form
.Pa A.71 .
The source for that problem is
.Pa solutions/A.71.cpp .
Its tests are in
.Pa tests/A.71/ .
The compiled program and scratch output are below
.Pa .build/ .
.Pp
The normal cycle is:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
make new A 71
edit solutions/A.71.cpp
make run A 71
make bundle A 71
.Ed
.Pp
The command names are short because they are used often.
Their manual pages are not.
See
.Xr build 1
for compiling and bundling,
.Xr test 1
for probes, cases, benchmarks, and stress tests, and
.Xr data 1
for commands which consult Codeforces.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "CXXFLAGS"
.It Ev CXX
The C++ compiler.
The default is
.Cm g++ .
.It Ev STD
The language standard.
The default is
.Cm gnu++20 .
.It Ev CXXFLAGS
Compiler flags.
The default is an optimized local build with warnings and
.Dv LOCAL
defined.
.It Ev CHECK
If set to
.Cm 1 ,
enables the checked build used by
.Cm make check .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width ".Pa tests/A.71/case-1.out"
.It Pa solutions/A.71.cpp
The source submitted after bundling.
.It Pa tests/A.71/case-1.in
Input for a saved test case.
.It Pa tests/A.71/case-1.out
Expected output for the same test case.
.It Pa template.cpp
Copied by
.Cm new
when a new source file is made.
.It Pa include/
Headers available to local builds and inlined by
.Cm bundle
when included with quotes.
.It Pa .build/
Compiled programs, probe output, benchmark output, API cache, and stress
failures.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
make new A 71
make run A 71
make check A 71
make probe A 71 big.in
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr build 1 ,
.Xr data 1 ,
.Xr test 1
